## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge caching behavior, tail latency, and backpressure under regional surge—a practical beginner scenario for performance testing.

## Key Concepts
- Edge caching and cache warming
- Tail latency (p95/p99)
- API gateway backpressure and circuit breakers
- Regional autoscaling and cost/latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = {
  scenarios: {
    regionalSurge: { executor: 'ramping-vus', startVUs: 0, stages: [ { duration: '2m', target: 50 }, { duration: '8m', target: 200 } ] }
  }
};
export default function () {
  http.get('https://region-A.example.com/pricing');
  http.post('https://region-A.example.com/book', JSON.stringify({}), { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  sleep(0.5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would network jitter influence your test results and how would you compensate for it?
- What signals would you use to decide if the edge cache warming was successful?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-time chat imposes tight latency budgets and backpressure handling under bursty activity and regional split. This probes workload modeling, autoscaling behavior, and resilience.

## Key Concepts
- WebSocket throughput and latency budgets
- Backpressure and queueing behavior
- Regional load testing and latency variance
- Autoscaling thresholds and warm-up times
- Resilience testing with failover

## Code Example
```javascript
// k6 script skeleton to establish WebSocket connections and message bursts
import ws from 'k6/ws';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
export default function () {
  const url = 'wss://chat.example.com/ws';
  const res = ws.connect(url, {}, function (socket) {
    socket.on('open', function () { socket.send(JSON.stringify({type:'join', room:'room1'})); });
    socket.on('message', function (data) { /* handle */ });
    for (let i=0; i<100; i++) { socket.send(JSON.stringify({type:'message', text:'hi'})); }
  });
  check(res, { 'connected': (r)=> r && r.status === 101 });
  sleep(1);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and isolate network variance impact on latency across regions?
- What autoscaling strategy would you choose for WS brokers and message queues under bursty traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates expertise in serverless architecture performance testing, end-to-end latency budgeting, autoscaling configuration, and observability for a complex checkout flow with multiple services and caching layers.

## Key Concepts

- Serverless latency characteristics and cold start mitigation
- Provisioned concurrency vs. dynamic autoscaling trade-offs
- End-to-end latency budgeting and P99 SLO management
- Cache effectiveness measurement and temperature state impact
- Failure injection and resilience testing patterns
- Capacity planning and scaling threshold validation

## Code Example

```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check } from 'k6';

export let options = {
  stages: [{ duration: '10m', target: 20000 }],
  thresholds: {
    'http_req_duration': ['p(99) < 300'],
    'cache_hit_ratio': ['> 0.8']
  }
};

export default function() {
  const response = http.post('https://api.checkout.com/process', {
    items: generateCart(),
    payment: generatePaymentMethod()
  });

  check(response, {
    'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200,
    'latency under 300ms': (r) => r.timings.duration < 300
  });
}
```

